---
description: SkyGround science and student privacy constraints for the public app
alwaysApply: true
---
Honor user instructions above project preferences. Product notes live in the private repository, not here.
- Distinguish above-horizon, near-overhead, Earth-satellite subpoint, instrument footprint, and thematic connection.
- Planets and the Moon use the astronomy adapter. They have no artificial-satellite ground anchor.
- Compute in UTC. Keep element epoch, snapshot fetch time, and calculation time separate.
- No accounts, analytics, student location history, or unexpected permissions.
- No geolocation in URLs, logs, persistent storage, repositories, or exported student work.
- Never poll CelesTrak from a student's browser. Shared ingestion stops on errors and does not retry automatically.
- Keep keys out of frontend assets.
- Do not infer historic events or mission relationships from proximity alone.
- Student media, news, and events need provenance, rights, and grade review before they appear.
- Use safe text rendering and validated HTTPS links.
- Keep list alternatives, focus, contrast, touch targets, and empty states.
- Add numerical tests for real sky calculations. Pin dependency versions and commit the lockfile.
- Sky angular selection and an Earth geographic area are different inputs.
- No required commercial sky engine, paid planet API, or fabricated provider data.
